  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn ichidan verb. The variant {禁|きん}ずる (classical form) also exists but {禁|きん}じる is standard in modern Japanese.\n\nSense 2 almost always appears in the fixed pattern ～を{禁|きん}じ{得|え}ない (cannot suppress, cannot help but feel). This is a formal, written expression.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {喫煙|きつえん}を{禁|きん}じる: to prohibit smoking\n- {法律|ほうりつ}で{禁|きん}じる: to prohibit by law\n- {涙|なみだ}を{禁|きん}じ{得|え}ない: cannot hold back tears\n- {驚|おどろ}きを{禁|きん}じ{得|え}ない: cannot help but be amazed",
